        ⭐ WHAT U4 AND U5 SAY TOGETHER. U4 alone would also be scored green
           by a mechanism that forced UTF-8 unconditionally, which would be
           a bug: a program run under LANG=C asked for a single-byte locale
           and must get one. U5 is the row that can fail for that reason.
        ⚠ AND THE AXIS IS ONE AXIS. This closes the environment-default
           codeset and says nothing about collation, message catalogues or
           any other locale category: C.UTF-8 is the C locale with a UTF-8
           charset, not a full locale.

